sections:

#### prop_section ####
kind: proposition
----
statement: The square on the straight line which produces with a medial area a medial whole, if applied to a rational straight line, produces as breadth a sixth apotome.
----
proof:

Let {AB} be the straight line which produces with a medial area a medial whole, and {CD} a rational straight line, and to {CD} let {CE|CEh} be applied equal to the square on {AB} and producing {CF} as breadth.

I say that {CF} is a sixth apotome.

Let {BG|GB} be the annex to {AB}. Then {AG} and {GB} are straight lines incommensurable in square which make the sum of the squares on them medial, twice the rectangle {AG} by {GB} medial, and the sum of the squares on {AG} and {GB} incommensurable with twice the rectangle {AG} by {GB}. [!just X.78]

<figure class="diagram">
<canvas id="canvas_0" width="370" height="180" tabindex="0"></canvas>
<noscript><img alt="X.102 diagram" src="propX102.gif"/></noscript>
<script type="text/javascript">
    // Joyce's figure (X.101's): AB with its annex BG on the line AG, the
    // rational line CD, and on it CE (DCFE) equal to the square on AB,
    // overlaid by FKHE (completing CH, the square on AG) and HKML (KL, the
    // square on BG), all random-faced, with N bisecting FM and the parallel
    // NO.
    // Added, all hidden at rest: solid twins ABs, GBs (initiallyHidden) so
    // AB stands alone before G and the annex is produced from B; transparent
    // targets AB, GB, CF, CK, KM, CM, FM, EF (;0;0;0); faceless, strokeless
    // targets CEh (twin of the random-faced DCFE, which would be raised over
    // its neighbours when lit, #140), CHh, KLh, CLh, FLh, FOh, NLh for the
    // rectangles the text names, reached with the display override
    // ({CE|CEh}). No angle is called right, so no markers.
    //
    // Draggables (checked against the bundle): A, B, G, C, D (line sliders)
    // and the offscreen frees. C and D arrive with "and CD a rational
    // straight line", G with the annex, so all three are deferred. F, E, K,
    // H, M, L, N, O are derived and listed per slide.
    var GIVEN = ["A","B","AB","ABs"];
    var RAT   = GIVEN.concat(["C","D","CD"]);
    var APPL  = RAT.concat(["F","E","DCFE","CEh","CF"]);
    var ANNEX = APPL.concat(["G","GB","GBs"]);
    var WHOLE = ANNEX.concat(["AG"]);
    var CHS   = WHOLE.concat(["K","H","FKHE","CHh","CK"]);
    var SQS   = CHS.concat(["M","L","HKML","KLh","KM"]);
    var CLS   = SQS.concat(["CLh","CM"]);
    var REM   = CLS.concat(["FLh","FM"]);
    var FES   = REM.concat(["EF"]);
    var ALL   = FES.concat(["N","O","NO","FOh","NLh"]);
    geomlib.init({
        canvasid: "canvas_0",
        background: "35,19,100",
        title: "X.102",
        elements: [
            "A0;point;free;-1000,40;0;0",
            "A3;point;free;1000,40;0;0",
            "C0;point;free;40,-1000;0;0",
            "C3;point;free;40,1000;0;0",
            "A;point;lineSlider;A0,A3,130,0",
            "B;point;lineSlider;A0,A3,200,0",
            "C;point;lineSlider;C0,C3,0,80",
            "D;point;lineSlider;C0,C3,0,150",
            "CD;line;connect;C,D",
            "F';point;parallelogram;C,A0,A3;0;0",
            "F;point;proportion;C,D,A,B,A,B,C,F'",
            "E;point;parallelogram;D,C,F",
            "DCFE;polygon;quadrilateral;D,C,F,E;0;0;black;random",
            "G;point;lineSlider;A0,A3,260,0",
            "AG;line;connect;A,G",
            "K;point;proportion;C,D,A,G,A,G,C,F'",
            "H;point;parallelogram;D,C,K",
            "FKHE;polygon;quadrilateral;F,K,H,E;0;0;black;random",
            "M;point;proportion;C,D,B,G,B,G,K,F'",
            "L;point;parallelogram;D,C,M",
            "HKML;polygon;quadrilateral;H,K,M,L;0;0;black;random",
            "N;point;midpoint;F,M",
            "O;point;parallelogram;D,C,N",
            "NO;line;connect;N,O",
            // Slide-only twins and highlight targets.
            "ABs;line;connect;A,B",
            "GBs;line;connect;B,G",
            "AB;line;connect;A,B;0;0;0",
            "GB;line;connect;G,B;0;0;0",
            "CF;line;connect;C,F;0;0;0",
            "CK;line;connect;C,K;0;0;0",
            "KM;line;connect;K,M;0;0;0",
            "CM;line;connect;C,M;0;0;0",
            "FM;line;connect;F,M;0;0;0",
            "EF;line;connect;E,F;0;0;0",
            "CEh;polygon;quadrilateral;D,C,F,E;0;0;0;0",
            "CHh;polygon;quadrilateral;D,C,K,H;0;0;0;0",
            "KLh;polygon;quadrilateral;H,K,M,L;0;0;0;0",
            "CLh;polygon;quadrilateral;D,C,M,L;0;0;0;0",
            "FLh;polygon;quadrilateral;E,F,M,L;0;0;0;0",
            "FOh;polygon;quadrilateral;E,F,N,O;0;0;0;0",
            "NLh;polygon;quadrilateral;O,N,M,L;0;0;0;0"
        ],
        initiallyHidden: ["ABs","GBs"],
        deferDraggables: ["C","D","G"],
        slides: [
            { text: "“The square on the straight line which produces with a medial area a medial whole,",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["AB"],
              justifications: [{ ref: "X.102" }] },
            { text: "if applied to a rational straight line, produces as breadth a sixth apotome.”",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["CD","CEh","CF"] },
            { text: "Let {AB} be the straight line which produces with a medial area a medial whole,",
              visible: GIVEN,
              highlighted: ["AB"] },
            { text: "and {CD} a rational straight line,",
              visible: RAT,
              highlighted: ["CD"],
              transition: { animations: [
                  { elem: "CD", name: geomlib.A.Line.straightEdgeConnect } ] } },
            { text: "and to {CD} let {CE|CEh} be applied equal to the square on {AB} and producing {CF} as breadth.",
              visible: APPL,
              highlighted: ["CD","AB","CF"],
              transition: { animations: [
                  { elem: "DCFE", name: geomlib.A.Polygon.outlineAndFill } ] } },
            { text: "I say that {CF} is a sixth apotome.",
              visible: APPL,
              highlighted: ["CF"] },
            { text: "Let {BG|GB} be the annex to {AB}.",
              visible: ANNEX,
              highlighted: ["GB","AB"],
              transition: { mode: "cascade", animations: [
                  { elem: "GBs", name: geomlib.A.Line.straightEdgeExtend },
                  { elem: "G",   name: geomlib.A.Point.appear } ] } },
            { text: "Then {AG} and {GB} are straight lines incommensurable in square which make the sum of the squares on them medial,",
              visible: WHOLE,
              highlighted: ["AG","GB"] },
            { text: "twice the rectangle {AG} by {GB} medial,",
              visible: WHOLE,
              highlighted: ["AG","GB"] },
            { text: "and the sum of the squares on {AG} and {GB} incommensurable with twice the rectangle {AG} by {GB}.",
              visible: WHOLE,
              highlighted: ["AG","GB"],
              justifications: [{ claim: "AB makes with a medial area a medial whole", ref: "X.78" }] },
            { text: "Now to {CD} apply {CH|CHh} equal to the square on {AG} and producing {CK} as breadth,",
              visible: CHS,
              highlighted: ["CD","AG","CK"],
              transition: { animations: [
                  { elem: "FKHE", name: geomlib.A.Polygon.outlineAndFill } ] } },
            { text: "and {KL|KLh} equal to the square on {BG|GB}.",
              visible: SQS,
              highlighted: ["GB"],
              transition: { animations: [
                  { elem: "HKML", name: geomlib.A.Polygon.outlineAndFill } ] } },
            { text: "Then the whole {CL|CLh} equals the sum of the squares on {AG} and {GB}.",
              visible: CLS,
              highlighted: ["CLh","AG","GB"] },
            { text: "Therefore {CL|CLh} is also medial.",
              visible: CLS,
              highlighted: ["CLh"] },
            { text: "And it is applied to the rational straight line {CD} producing {CM} as breadth,",
              visible: CLS,
              highlighted: ["CLh","CD","CM"] },
            { text: "therefore {CM} is rational and incommensurable in length with {CD}.",
              visible: CLS,
              highlighted: ["CM","CD"],
              justifications: [{ claim: "CM rational, incommensurable with CD", ref: "X.22" }] },
            { text: "Since {CL|CLh} equals the sum of the squares on {AG} and {GB},",
              visible: CLS,
              highlighted: ["CLh","AG","GB"] },
            { text: "and, in these, {CE|CEh} equals the square on {AB},",
              visible: CLS,
              highlighted: ["CEh","AB"] },
            { text: "therefore the remainder {FL|FLh} equals twice the rectangle {AG} by {GB}.",
              visible: REM,
              highlighted: ["FLh","AG","GB"],
              justifications: [{ claim: "AG² + GB² = 2 AG·GB + AB²", ref: "II.7" }] },
            { text: "And twice the rectangle {AG} by {GB} is medial, therefore {FL|FLh} is also medial.",
              visible: REM,
              highlighted: ["AG","GB","FLh"] },
            { text: "And it is applied to the rational straight line {FE|EF} producing {FM} as breadth,",
              visible: FES,
              highlighted: ["FLh","EF","FM"] },
            { text: "therefore {FM} is rational and incommensurable in length with {CD}.",
              visible: FES,
              highlighted: ["FM","CD"],
              justifications: [{ claim: "FM rational, incommensurable with CD", ref: "X.22" }] },
            { text: "Since the sum of the squares on {AG} and {GB} is incommensurable with twice the rectangle {AG} by {GB},",
              visible: FES,
              highlighted: ["AG","GB"] },
            { text: "{CL|CLh} equals the sum of the squares on {AG} and {GB},",
              visible: FES,
              highlighted: ["CLh","AG","GB"] },
            { text: "and {FL|FLh} equals twice the rectangle {AG} by {GB},",
              visible: FES,
              highlighted: ["FLh","AG","GB"] },
            { text: "therefore {CL|CLh} is incommensurable with {FL|FLh}.",
              visible: FES,
              highlighted: ["CLh","FLh"] },
            { text: "But {CL|CLh} is to {FL|FLh} as {CM} is to {MF|FM},",
              visible: FES,
              highlighted: ["CLh","FLh","CM","FM"],
              justifications: [{ claim: "CL : FL = CM : MF", ref: "VI.1" }] },
            { text: "therefore {CM} is incommensurable in length with {MF|FM}. And both are rational.",
              visible: FES,
              highlighted: ["CM","FM"],
              justifications: [{ claim: "CM, MF incommensurable", ref: "X.11" }] },
            { text: "Therefore {CM} and {MF|FM} are rational straight lines commensurable in square only,",
              visible: FES,
              highlighted: ["CM","FM"] },
            { text: "therefore {CF} is an apotome.",
              visible: FES,
              highlighted: ["CF"],
              justifications: [{ claim: "CF an apotome", ref: "X.73" }] },
            { text: "I say next that it is also a sixth apotome.",
              visible: FES,
              highlighted: ["CF"] },
            { text: "Since {FL|FLh} equals twice the rectangle {AG} by {GB},",
              visible: FES,
              highlighted: ["FLh","AG","GB"] },
            { text: "bisect {FM} at {N}, and draw {NO} through {N} parallel to {CD},",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["FM","CD"],
              transition: { mode: "cascade", animations: [
                  { elem: "N",  name: geomlib.A.Point.appear },
                  { elem: "NO", name: geomlib.A.Line.straightEdgeConnect } ] } },
            { text: "therefore each of the rectangles {FO|FOh} and {NL|NLh} equals the rectangle {AG} by {GB}.",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["FOh","NLh","AG","GB"] },
            { text: "And, since {AG} and {GB} are incommensurable in square,",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["AG","GB"] },
            { text: "therefore the square on {AG} is incommensurable with the square on {GB}.",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["AG","GB"] },
            { text: "But {CH|CHh} equals the square on {AG}, and {KL|KLh} equals the square on {GB},",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["CHh","AG","KLh","GB"] },
            { text: "therefore {CH|CHh} is incommensurable with {KL|KLh}.",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["CHh","KLh"] },
            { text: "But {CH|CHh} is to {KL|KLh} as {CK} is to {KM},",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["CHh","KLh","CK","KM"],
              justifications: [{ claim: "CH : KL = CK : KM", ref: "VI.1" }] },
            { text: "therefore {CK} is incommensurable with {KM}.",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["CK","KM"],
              justifications: [{ claim: "CK, KM incommensurable", ref: "X.11" }] },
            { text: "Since the rectangle {AG} by {GB} is a mean proportional between the squares on {AG} and {GB},",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["AG","GB"] },
            { text: "{CH|CHh} equals the square on {AG}, {KL|KLh} equals the square on {GB},",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["CHh","AG","KLh","GB"] },
            { text: "and {NL|NLh} equals the rectangle {AG} by {GB},",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["NLh","AG","GB"] },
            { text: "therefore {NL|NLh} is also a mean proportional between {CH|CHh} and {KL|KLh}.",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["NLh","CHh","KLh"] },
            { text: "Therefore {CH|CHh} is to {NL|NLh} as {NL|NLh} is to {KL|KLh}.",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["CHh","NLh","KLh"] },
            { text: "And for the same reason as before the square on {CM} is greater than the square on {MF|FM}",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["CM","FM"] },
            { text: "by the square on a straight line incommensurable with {CM}.",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["CM"],
              justifications: [{ claim: "CM² − MF² incommensurable with CM", ref: "X.18" }] },
            { text: "And neither of them is commensurable with the rational straight line {CD} set out,",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["CM","FM","CD"] },
            { text: "therefore {CF} is a sixth apotome.",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["CF"],
              justifications: [{ claim: "CF a sixth apotome", ref: "X.Def.III.6" }] },
            { text: "Therefore, the square on the straight line which produces with a medial area a medial whole,",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["AB"] },
            { text: "if applied to a rational straight line, produces as breadth a sixth apotome.",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["CD","CEh","CF"],
              justifications: [{ ref: "Q.E.D." }] }
        ],
        resolveJustification: function(ref) {
            if (ref === "X.102") return "#prop";
            return (window.eucrefs && window.eucrefs[ref]) || null;
        }
    });

    // Per-page citation lookup for the slideshow's resolveJustification.
    window.eucrefs = (window.eucrefs || {});
    Object.assign(window.eucrefs, {
        "II.7":        "/elements/books/bookII/propositions/propII7/",
        "VI.1":        "/elements/books/bookVI/propositions/propVI1/",
        "X.11":        "/elements/books/bookX/propositions/propX11/",
        "X.18":        "/elements/books/bookX/propositions/propX18/",
        "X.22":        "/elements/books/bookX/propositions/propX22/",
        "X.73":        "/elements/books/bookX/propositions/propX73/",
        "X.78":        "/elements/books/bookX/propositions/propX78/",
        "X.Def.III.6": "/elements/books/bookX/definitions/defX.III.6/"
    });
</script>
</figure>

Now to {CD} apply {CH|CHh} equal to the square on {AG} and producing {CK} as breadth, and {KL|KLh} equal to the square on {BG|GB}. Then the whole {CL|CLh} equals the sum of the squares on {AG} and {GB}. Therefore {CL|CLh} is also medial.

And it is applied to the rational straight line {CD} producing {CM} as breadth, therefore {CM} is rational and incommensurable in length with {CD}. [!just X.22]

Since {CL|CLh} equals the sum of the squares on {AG} and {GB}, and, in these, {CE|CEh} equals the square on {AB}, therefore the remainder {FL|FLh} equals twice the rectangle {AG} by {GB}. And twice the rectangle {AG} by {GB} is medial, therefore {FL|FLh} is also medial. [!just II.7]

And it is applied to the rational straight line {FE|EF} producing {FM} as breadth, therefore {FM} is rational and incommensurable in length with {CD}. [!just X.22]

Since the sum of the squares on {AG} and {GB} is incommensurable with twice the rectangle {AG} by {GB}, {CL|CLh} equals the sum of the squares on {AG} and {GB}, and {FL|FLh} equals twice the rectangle {AG} by {GB}, therefore {CL|CLh} is incommensurable with {FL|FLh}.

But {CL|CLh} is to {FL|FLh} as {CM} is to {MF|FM}, therefore {CM} is incommensurable in length with {MF|FM}. And both are rational. [!just VI.1, X.11]

Therefore {CM} and {MF|FM} are rational straight lines commensurable in square only, therefore {CF} is an apotome. [!just X.73]

I say next that it is also a sixth apotome.

Since {FL|FLh} equals twice the rectangle {AG} by {GB}, bisect {FM} at {N}, and draw {NO} through {N} parallel to {CD}, therefore each of the rectangles {FO|FOh} and {NL|NLh} equals the rectangle {AG} by {GB}.

And, since {AG} and {GB} are incommensurable in square, therefore the square on {AG} is incommensurable with the square on {GB}.

But {CH|CHh} equals the square on {AG}, and {KL|KLh} equals the square on {GB}, therefore {CH|CHh} is incommensurable with {KL|KLh}.

But {CH|CHh} is to {KL|KLh} as {CK} is to {KM}, therefore {CK} is incommensurable with {KM}. [!just VI.1, X.11]

Since the rectangle {AG} by {GB} is a mean proportional between the squares on {AG} and {GB}, {CH|CHh} equals the square on {AG}, {KL|KLh} equals the square on {GB}, and {NL|NLh} equals the rectangle {AG} by {GB}, therefore {NL|NLh} is also a mean proportional between {CH|CHh} and {KL|KLh}. Therefore {CH|CHh} is to {NL|NLh} as {NL|NLh} is to {KL|KLh}.

And for the same reason as before the square on {CM} is greater than the square on {MF|FM} by the square on a straight line incommensurable with {CM}. [!just X.18]

And neither of them is commensurable with the rational straight line {CD} set out, therefore {CF} is a sixth apotome. [!just X.Def.III.6]

Therefore, *the square on the straight line which produces with a medial area a medial whole, if applied to a rational straight line, produces as breadth a sixth apotome.*

<div class="qed">Q.E.D.</div>
